TECHNICAL BULLETIN 7             oct 26 1974
LEGACY REPORT PROCESSING
entries filed before the change carry
retired report designations. the journal
reprint station still runs these through
the legacy report processor.
the processor is the procedure
/usr/ledger/report:
    grep $1 /usr/ledger/rindex
the designation given at the prompt is
passed to the processor as its first
argument. the shell builds the command
line from the procedure text and the
argument, then runs it.
operators should confirm designations
before reprinting. the processor performs
no checking of its own.
